---
import { SAAS_MONTHLY_GBP } from '@/lib/seo/defaults';
---

<section class="booksy-alt__section" aria-labelledby="booksy-alt-decision-title">
  <div class="booksy-alt__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="booksy-alt__intro">
      <h2 id="booksy-alt-decision-title" class="booksy-alt__h2">
        So, which one is right for your barbershop?
      </h2>
    </header>

    <div class="booksy-alt-panels">
      <article class="booksy-alt-panel">
        <p class="booksy-alt-panel__label">BOOKSY MAY SUIT YOU IF…</p>
        <ul class="booksy-alt-panel__list">
          <li>Marketplace discovery is an important part of how you find clients.</li>
          <li>You want access to the wider Booksy consumer ecosystem.</li>
          <li>You prefer a mature platform with a broad set of built-in business tools.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="booksy-alt-panel booksy-alt-panel--kersivo">
        <p class="booksy-alt-panel__label">KERSIVO MAY SUIT YOU IF…</p>
        <ul class="booksy-alt-panel__list">
          <li>Your barbershop brand should remain the main customer touchpoint.</li>
          <li>You want your own website and standard domain included.</li>
          <li>You want clients booking through an experience centred on your business.</li>
          <li>
            You prefer a £{SAAS_MONTHLY_GBP}/month per-location model with 0% KERSIVO commission.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="booksy-alt-closing">
      Neither model is right for every barbershop. The question is what you want your booking system
      to do for your brand.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
